# CVE-2026-14456 — openssl: Denial of Service via unbounded memory growth in
# the QUIC server (HIGH, alpine pkg "openssl").
#
# Why ignored: the finding lives in the base images' libcrypto3/libssl3
# (openssl 3.5.7-r0). The fix (3.5.8-r0) exists upstream, but the
# golang:1.26.6-alpine and alpine 3.24.1 runtime images have not refreshed
# yet. GuardianWAF builds with CGO_ENABLED=0, so the WAF binary does not link
# openssl, and the project does not run an openssl QUIC server — exposure is
# limited to the base image package set, not to the shipped firewall.
#
# Integration: both scanning jobs (ci.yml trivy-docker base-image scan,
# scripts/supply-chain-smoke.sh) mount this file at /.trivyignore inside the
# Trivy container (Trivy 0.68.1 reads the ignore file from the container CWD).
# Any NEW CVE still fails both gates — this suppresses exactly one ID.
#
# EXPIRES: 2026-10-31
# On expiry the governance test TestTrivyIgnoreEntriesNotExpired fails until
# this entry is removed — correct once upstream images ship openssl >=
# 3.5.8-r0 (re-scan to confirm, then delete this file and the mounts).
CVE-2026-14456

# AVD-KSV-0109 — ConfigMap stores secrets in key(s) or value(s) (HIGH).
#
# Why ignored: the finding matches the key NAME "secret" inside the embedded
# guardianwaf.yaml template in contrib/k8s/cluster-configmap.yaml. The value
# is a placeholder (${GWAF_CLUSTER_SECRET}) substituted at runtime from the
# guardianwaf-cluster Secret — the manifest deliberately never inlines the
# key. This is the documented correct pattern; the check is shape-based.
#
# Scope note: .trivyignore entries are ID-scoped, so this suppresses ALL
# KSV-0109 findings repo-wide. Acceptable while the only finding is this
# template; re-evaluate if new ConfigMaps appear.
#
# EXPIRES: 2026-10-31
AVD-KSV-0109
